  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "The current best (config_006: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted; acc=0.713) has established that multiprofile + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion is the strongest design. However, the image encoder has never been varied—all 8 completed experiments use resnet50, leaving a major design dimension completely unexplored. config_020 is identical to config_006 except it swaps resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l, isolating the effect of the image representation while holding all other settings at their best-known values. This is the highest-information single-variable experiment available: if ViT improves performance, it confirms the image encoder is a productive axis to further exploit; if it does not, it tells us resnet50 is already near-sufficient and we should redirect budget toward RNA encoder or other dimensions. No other available configuration tests this critical unexplored axis with a single clean change from the current best."
}

